      "id": "practice/maths-a-level/maths-statistics-year-1/ch5/exam/q32",
      "status": "worked",
      "method": "Estimate from class midpoints; interpolate for the standard-deviation thresholds.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "explanation": "<span class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\sum fw=366;\\quad\\sum fw^2=4975.5;\\quad n=30\"></span><span class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\bar x=\\frac{366}{30}=12.2\"></span><span class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\sigma=\\sqrt{\\frac{4975.5}{30}-\\left(\\frac{366}{30}\\right)^2}\\approx4.12432\"></span>"
        },
        {
          "explanation": "<span class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\bar w-\\sigma\\approx8.07568;\\quad\\bar w+\\sigma\\approx16.32432\"></span><span class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"P(|w-\\bar w|&gt;\\sigma)\\approx\\frac{7+5(0.07568/3)+4+8(0.67568/3)}{30}\"></span><span class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\approx0.430932\"></span><p>Rounding the thresholds to 8.1 and 16.3 gives 13/30≈0.433, as in the supplied answer. “From the mean” is interpreted as either side, not just above.</p>"
        },
        {
          "explanation": "<p>Assume observations are uniformly distributed within each class.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "solutionHtml": "<p>Estimate from class midpoints; interpolate for the standard-deviation thresholds.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><span class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\sum fw=366;\\quad\\sum fw^2=4975.5;\\quad n=30\"></span><span class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\bar x=\\frac{366}{30}=12.2\"></span><span class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\sigma=\\sqrt{\\frac{4975.5}{30}-\\left(\\frac{366}{30}\\right)^2}\\approx4.12432\"></span></li><li><span class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\bar w-\\sigma\\approx8.07568;\\quad\\bar w+\\sigma\\approx16.32432\"></span><span class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"P(|w-\\bar w|&gt;\\sigma)\\approx\\frac{7+5(0.07568/3)+4+8(0.67568/3)}{30}\"></span><span class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"\\approx0.430932\"></span><p>Rounding the thresholds to 8.1 and 16.3 gives 13/30≈0.433, as in the supplied answer. “From the mean” is interpreted as either side, not just above.</p></li><li><p>Assume observations are uniformly distributed within each class.</p></li></ol>",
